description:
src/methods/mod.rs:40 — MetadataChangesParams derives only Debug, Default, Serialize. A caller running a paginated change-fetching loop:

    let params = MetadataChangesParams { filter_related_type: Some(\"Email\".into()), .. Default::default() };
    let mut state = since_state;
    loop {
        let resp = sc.metadata_changes(&state, Some(256), Some(params.clone())).await?;
        //                                                          ^^^^^^^^ does not compile
        if !resp.has_more_changes { break; }
        state = resp.new_state;
    }

…cannot reuse the params because metadata_changes takes 'params: Option<MetadataChangesParams>' (by value, line metadata.rs:70). The caller must construct a fresh MetadataChangesParams every iteration, which means materialising the filter_metadata_type Vec<String> from scratch each time.

The contract claim (in metadata_changes's doc-comment, line 60-65) that 'clients that use these filters MUST re-use the same filter values across subsequent calls' is undermined when the only ergonomic way to do that is to clone — and the type doesn't support clone.

Fix: add Clone to the derive. Cost: filter_metadata_type clone is O(n) on the type names, but n is bounded by the number of @type values the caller cares about (typically small — Annotation, ImapMetadata, WebDavMetadata are the only three currently defined). Acceptable.

Workspace-wide: canonical EmailGetParams in mail-client also lacks Clone. Propagate.

Lower-priority note: also missing PartialEq, Eq, Hash — but those are taste, mark as opinion if added. Clone is the only one with an engineering basis.
